{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nusing VI = vector<int>;\n\nconst ll MOD = 1000000007;\nconst ll MOD2 = 998244353;\n\nVI pos[7];\nll pw[15], s[7];\nll cnt2, n;\nint ans = 0;\n\ninline ll mod_add(ll a, ll b, ll mod) {\n    return (a + b) % mod;\n}\n\ninline ll mod_sub(ll a, ll b, ll mod) {\n    return ((a - b) % mod + mod) % mod;\n}\n\ninline ll mod_mul(ll a, ll b, ll mod) {\n    return (a * b) % mod;\n}\n\nint query(int fixpre, ll val) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    for (int d = 0; d < 7; ++d) {\n        ll offset = mod_sub(val, 1LL * fixpre * pw[d], MOD2);\n        int p = lower_bound(pos[d].begin(), pos[d].end(), MOD2 - offset) - pos[d].begin();\n        res = mod_add(res, mod_add(s[d], mod_sub(mod_mul(offset, (ll)pos[d].size(), MOD2), \n            mod_mul(MOD2, (ll)(pos[d].size() - p), MOD2), MOD2), MOD), MOD);\n    }\n    return (int)(res % MOD);\n}\n\nvoid dfs(int val, int d) {\n    int x = (cnt2 - val + MOD2) % MOD2;\n    pos[d].push_back(x);\n    cnt2++;\n    s[d] = (s[d] + x) % MOD2;\n    if (d == 6) return;\n    for (int i = 0; i < 10; ++i) {\n        dfs(val * 10 + i, d + 1);\n    }\n}\n\nvoid dfs2(ll val) {\n    if (val * 1000000 + 999999 <= n && val * 10000000 > n) {\n        ans = (ans + query(val, cnt2 + 1)) % MOD;\n        cnt2 += cnt2;\n    } else {\n        cnt2++;\n        ll diff = mod_sub(cnt2, val, MOD2);\n        ans = (ans + (int)diff) % MOD;\n        int start = val ? 0 : 1;\n        for (int i = start; i < 10; ++i) {\n            if (val * 10 + i <= n) {\n                dfs2(val * 10 + i);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cnt2 = 0;\n    dfs(0, 0);\n    for (int i = 0; i < 7; ++i) {\n        sort(pos[i].begin(), pos[i].end());\n    }\n    pw[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i < 13; ++i) {\n        pw[i] = pw[i - 1] * 10;\n    }\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &n);\n    cnt2 = -1;\n    dfs2(0);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", ans);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport bisect\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nMOD2 = 998244353\n\npos = [[] for _ in range(7)]\npw = [0] * 15\ns = [0] * 7\ncnt2 = 0\nn = 0\nans = 0\n\ndef mod_add(a, b, mod):\n    return (a + b) % mod\n\ndef mod_sub(a, b, mod):\n    return ((a - b) % mod + mod) % mod\n\ndef mod_mul(a, b, mod):\n    return (a * b) % mod\n\ndef query(fixpre, val):\n    global pos, s, MOD2, MOD\n    res = 0\n    for d in range(7):\n        offset = mod_sub(val, fixpre * pw[d], MOD2)\n        # Find the first position where pos[d][i] >= (MOD2 - offset)\n        target = MOD2 - offset\n        p = bisect.bisect_left(pos[d], target)\n        size = len(pos[d])\n        term1 = s[d]\n        term2 = mod_sub(mod_mul(offset, size, MOD2), mod_mul(MOD2, size - p, MOD2), MOD2)\n        res = mod_add(res, mod_add(term1, term2, MOD), MOD)\n    return int(res % MOD)\n\ndef dfs(val, d):\n    global cnt2, pos, s, MOD2\n    x = (cnt2 - val + MOD2) % MOD2\n    pos[d].append(x)\n    cnt2 += 1\n    s[d] = (s[d] + x) % MOD2\n    if d == 6:\n        return\n    for i in range(10):\n        dfs(val * 10 + i, d + 1)\n\ndef dfs2(val):\n    global cnt2, ans, n, MOD2, MOD\n    if val * 1000000 + 999999 <= n and val * 10000000 > n:\n        ans = (ans + query(val, cnt2 + 1)) % MOD\n        cnt2 += cnt2\n    else:\n        cnt2 += 1\n        diff = mod_sub(cnt2, val, MOD2)\n        ans = (ans + int(diff)) % MOD\n        start = 0 if val else 1\n        for i in range(start, 10):\n            if val * 10 + i <= n:\n                dfs2(val * 10 + i)\n\ndef main():\n    global cnt2, n, ans, pw\n    cnt2 = 0\n    dfs(0, 0)\n    for i in range(7):\n        pos[i].sort()\n    pw[0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, 13):\n        pw[i] = pw[i - 1] * 10\n    n = int(sys.stdin.readline().strip())\n    cnt2 = -1\n    dfs2(0)\n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00018737945356406271, -9.536738616588991e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0037041164468973875, -0.10145203769207001, -0.06995179504156113, -0.026023590937256813, -0.0012265071272850037, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.011050808243453503, -0.22615833580493927, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00010907054820563644, 0.0, -0.00018249277491122484, 0.0, 0.0, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.006777428206988e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.125986263010418e-06, -8.106198947643861e-06, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -5.960446742392378e-06, -4.887569048150908e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -2.47952248173533e-05, -0.00033706706017255783, -0.03652980551123619, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.001844849088229239, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.1723164940776